A||||1||mrfiero||Where to go in San Jose...||||10||
Z||000000||mrfiero||08-16-2001||01:58 AM||||I just got home from a long road trip, well actually two road trips......the last one was to the San Francisco area.<P>Several weeks ago I completely rebuilt my front suspension and was waiting to do the rear before getting an alignment.  This was a mistake!  I chewed up the front tires in no time.  <P>I was in the San Jose area (Campbell, to be exact) and saw a Goodyear tire store.  Since I have a Goodyear credit card I went in to see about some tires and an alignment......this was at 4pm and they closed at 6pm.  The grand total was about $478, which was more than I had available on the card.  The manager decided to knock off $76 so I could afford everything!  Talk about a nice guy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>They squeezed me in for an alignment and got me out by 6pm.  To top it all off.....the alignment guy has worked on Fieros and DIDN'T COMPLAIN about having to align one.....talk about good luck!  I have yet to find a place (at least in Denver) that can do a good alignment, let alone not complain about how hard Fieros are to deal with.  <P>After putting over 1400 miles on it I can honestly say it is the best alignmemt I have had on any of my Fieros to date.  It tracks nice and straight, doesn't wander or pull, etc......basically it's how it SHOULD be all of the time.<P>At any rate, I figured I would give them a plug......it's the Goodyear tire store at 1790 S. Bascom Ave. in Campbell, California.  <P>If you are in the area and need tires or an alignment give them a try.<P>BTW......I got the Eagle HP's and they are pretty decent tires (on sale for $75 apiece).<P>     ||||reg||10
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-16-2001||05:46 PM||||I've said it before, We have some good shops out here in the bay area!!!!!!<P>Hpoe you had a good time in our little city<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
